+4.  **Geometric Loss Calculation:** Compute $\mathcal{L}_{geo}$ by comparing $D_{rendered}$ with the estimated depth $D_i$ [S1].
+5.  **Normal Consistency:** Compute surface normals from the estimated depth map $D_i$ [G]. Align the Gaussian orientation (derived from the rotation quaternion or covariance matrix) with these normals to compute $\mathcal{L}_{norm}$ [G].
 6.  **Gaussian Pruning:** Remove Gaussians that exhibit incorrect depth values or large discrepancies between rendered and estimated depth, effectively cleaning up noise and artifacts common in sparse views [S1].
 7.  **Optional SDS Regularization:** To further encourage faithful results from novel viewpoints, apply Score Distillation Sampling (SDS) loss [S1]. This leverages a pre-trained diffusion model to provide additional geometric priors where multi-view cues are weak [S1].
 8.  **Optimization:** Update Gaussian parameters ($\mathbf{c}_j, \Sigma_j, \alpha_j, \mathbf{c}_{j,SH}$) using gradient descent to minimize $\mathcal{L}_{total}$ [S1].
 
+**Formulas:**
+The total loss function combines the standard photometric loss with geometric and normal consistency terms, following the shared principles of the parent family [G]:
+$$ \mathcal{L}_{total} = \mathcal{L}_{rgb} + \lambda_{geo} \mathcal{L}_{geo} + \lambda_{norm} \mathcal{L}_{norm} $$
+Where:
+*   $\mathcal{L}_{rgb}$ is the standard L1/SSIM photometric loss between rendered and input images [G].
+*   $\mathcal{L}_{geo}$ enforces positional consistency between Gaussian centers and the estimated depth [G].
+*   $\mathcal{L}_{norm}$ enforces normal consistency between Gaussian orientations and surface normals derived from the depth map [G].
+*   $\lambda_{geo}$ and $\lambda_{norm}$ are hyperparameters balancing photometric fidelity against geometric accuracy [S1].
+
